# Line endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows and runs on Linux, which is a
# combination that can produce a file that looks fine in an editor and fails
# on a server. A shell script with CRLF endings has a shebang of
# `#!/bin/bash\r`, and the kernel looks for an interpreter with a carriage
# return in its name, finds nothing, and the script never starts. Nothing
# reports a line-ending problem, because nothing can tell the difference
# between that and a missing interpreter.
#
# It has already happened once here: an edit through a Windows text API
# rewrote infra/user_data.sh with CRLF, and the next instance replacement
# would have booted a host whose bootstrap could not run at all.
#
# So: normalise text in the repository, and force LF on everything that is
# read by a Linux kernel, a shell, or a container.

* text=auto

*.sh            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.tf            text eol=lf
*.template      text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.jsx           text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.ini           text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# Keep binaries out of it.
*.pdf           binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.ico           binary
